course: dictionary
lesson: 15381
title: Specialised words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something was made or trained for one special job. «Specialised» is one of them. When you meet it, ask: specialised for what? The words around it give the clue. «The surgeon used specialised tools to mend the tiny bone.» Specialised tools are made for one particular job, so these tools were built for bone surgery.
explain: Specialised can also describe a person. «My aunt is a specialised doctor who only treats eyes.» The word only and the word eyes show that she trained for one particular area.
explain: Specialised is also the past tense of the verb specialise. «She specialised in history at school.» This means she focused her learning on one subject. In American English the spelling is specialized, but the meaning is the same.
explain: Science uses this idea too. Many cells in your body are specialised: each has a special shape for its own job, so it can do that job well.
fact: Specialised means made or trained for one particular job or purpose.
fact: As an adjective, «specialised» describes things like «specialised equipment» and people like «a specialised doctor».
fact: As the past of «specialise», it means focused on one subject: «she specialised in history».
fact: In science, specialised cells have a special shape for their job: red blood cells carry oxygen, nerve cells carry messages and root hair cells take in water.
fact: The American spelling is specialized; both spellings are used for the same word.
exercise: «The hospital has specialised equipment for babies born early.» What does specialised mean here? | Old and broken | Shiny and new | Very cheap | *Made for one particular job
exercise: «She specialised in art at college.» Which word means the same as specialised here? | Forgot | Ignored | Shouted | *Focused on one subject
exercise: Red blood cells are specialised. What does this tell you about them? | They are very big and heavy | They are all the same shape as nerve cells | They cannot move at all | *Each has a special shape for carrying oxygen
test: «The cook used a specialised knife only for cutting fish.» What does specialised mean? | *Used for one special job | Very sharp for every kind of food | Made of gold | Borrowed from a friend
test: Nerve cells are specialised. What is their special job? | Carry oxygen to the blood | *Carry messages around the body | Take in water from the soil | Store food in the leaves
exam: Jayden says specialised just means special. What is the better meaning? | Nice to look at | Covered in paint | *Made or trained for one particular job | Very old and rare
